ExecuteSimTalk [SimTalk]
Executes the source code, which you specify, in a Method.
Type
Function
Syntax
PlantSim.ExecuteSimTalk(SourceCode:string[, Parameter1, Parameter2, 
Parameter3]) -> any
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters.
• The parameter SourceCode of data type string designates the source code, which is going to be
executed in the Method.
When the source code of the method contains a parameter, you can enter this as the second parameter
into the method ExecuteSimTalk. The method ExecuteSimTalk then will return the return value of the
method.
• The optional parameters Parameter1, Parameter2 and Parameter3 allow to pass up to three arguments
to the SimTalk method contained in the first argument.
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
It is the return value of the Method.
Example
// JScript
var PlantSim = 
WScript.CreateObject("Tecnomatix.PlantSimulation.RemoteControl")
PlantSim.ExecuteSimTalk("->real; return 3.14159")
PlantSim.ExecuteSimTalk("param r:real->real; return r*r", 3.14159)
ExecuteSimTalk [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 14-213
