SimulationFinished [SimTalk]
At the end of a simulation run Plant Simulation triggers the event SimulationFinished. You can use it to
read the results of a simulation run.
SimulationFinished [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 14-233
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Example of a JScript
A JScript might look as follows:
var vbOKCancel = 1;
var vbCancel = 2;
var vbInformation = 64;
var Finished=false;
var WSHShell = new ActiveXObject("WScript.Shell");
var simple = 
WScript.CreateObject("Tecnomatix.PlantSimulation.RemoteControl1", 
"RemoteControl_");
simple.SetLicenseType("Runtime");
try
{
// Enter the path to a model file!
simple.LoadModel("C:\\Models\\Test.spp");
}
catch (e)
{
WScript.Echo("Could not load Model!");
WScript.Quit();
}
try
{
simple.SetValue(".Models.Model.Buffer.ProcTime", 700.0); } catch (e) {
r=WSHShell.Popup(e.description, 0, "Continue?", vbOKCancel + vbInformation);
if (r == vbCancel)
{
    simple.CloseModel();
    WScript.Quit();
}
}
simple.StartSimulation(".Models.Model.EventController");
if (simple.IsSimulationRunning())
WScript.Echo("Simulation is running!");
// Wait until simulation is finished
while (!Finished) WScript.Sleep(2000);
simple.CloseModel();
simple.Quit();
WScript.Quit();
function RemoteControl_SimulationFinished()
{
Example of a JScript
14-234 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

WScript.Echo("Simulation Finished!");
Finished = true;
}
function RemoteControl_SimTalkMessage(str) {
WScript.Echo(str);
}
